# Drafted by Gemini (R17 hugo), edited.

~ bark
set mr_hugo_barked
hugo [angry]: No loud feet on the stairs! Hugo keeps the quiet for the Matron!
Narrator: The ceiling timbers groan under a massive weight, and fine plaster dust sifts down into the violet light.
-> END

~ peace
Narrator: The giant kneels in the dark water beside the Matron's still form, his sewn eyelids trembling as his great fists strike the stone.
hugo [angry]: You broke the quiet. You hurt the little lady who took Hugo's bad dreams away. Hugo will crush your bones to meal!
* [Persuasion DC 20] Tell him she would not want this -> peace_one_ok | peace_fail
* [knows:remove_curse] Lift his curse with Remove Curse -> peace_curse
* Defend yourselves -> peace_fight

~ peace_one_ok
Narrator: His huge knuckles pop as his hands slowly unclench, the cold cavern water lapping against his wrists.
hugo [sad]: She hated loud noises. She told Hugo to be a gentle wall, never a storm.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Settle down now, big lad. A watchman holds his post without bringing the roof down.
-> peace_two

~ peace_two
hugo [weary]: Hugo carried the heavy pails. Hugo held the bad ones still so she could make them well. Did Hugo not do good?
* [Persuasion DC 17] Speak of what he did for her -> peace_three | peace_fail
* Defend yourselves -> peace_fight

~ peace_three
hugo [sad]: Hugo kept every promise. Even when the dark under the floor made Hugo's head ache, Hugo stayed by her door.
* [Persuasion DC 14] Tell him he can rest now -> peace_done | peace_fail
* Defend yourselves -> peace_fight

~ peace_curse
approve tobin_hayward +4 silas_vane +3 delphine_ravelle +3: You lifted the foul enchantment clouding Hugo's mind
set hugo_curse_lifted
Narrator: A warm breath of clean wind unwinds the foul enchantment round his brow, and the grey fog of the cavern seems to part.
hugo [afraid]: The buzzing in Hugo's head is gone. Why is it so cold down here? Little lady?
-> peace_done

~ peace_done
set hugo_fate = "gone"
set hugo_calmed
cutscene mr_hugo_grief
hugo [sad]: The bells are done ringing. Nobody needs a big door-stone anymore.
cutscene mr_hugo_grief_2
Narrator: He weeps like a lost child, his broad shoulders heaving until the dark water ripples from wall to wall, and then he rises.
hugo [weary]: Hugo will walk to the far edge of the hollow, where the reeds grow tall and no one asks for help. Hugo just wants the quiet.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Off the stage with no strings left on him. Mind the reeds, big fellow.
cutscene end
-> END

~ peace_fail
hugo [angry]: Lies! Bad, loud lies! Hugo will make the silence come back!
Narrator: His roar shakes loose wet stones from the grotto roof, though his feet stay rooted beside her cold hand.
-> peace

~ peace_fight
approve tobin_hayward -2 delphine_ravelle -2 lucan_houndstooth +1: You fought grieving Hugo instead of talking him down
set hugo_fate = "dead"
hugo [angry]: Sleep now, little lady! Hugo will clear the room!
combat mr_hugo_after
